hi my name is kanchan koya as the  founder of spice spice baby with a phd  in biomedicine i know that food can be  medicine what we eat plays a huge role  in our overall health so today i'm going  to show you how to make a gut health  boosting dinner and dessert that is as  good for you as it is delicious let's  get started  when we think about gut health we're  really thinking about the health of our  microbiome the microbiome is the  trillions of bacteria that live in our  guts these bacteria can be good  beneficial bacteria that do tremendously  useful things for our health if we feed  them the right foods  we're going to start with whole  coriander seeds when we're thinking  about gut health we also want to think  about managing inflammation and all of  the spices in this marinade are  inflammation fighters when you toast  these whole coriander seeds you're  waking up a lot of those beneficial  volatile compounds and now we're gonna  tip them into the mortar and pestle and  grind them up grinding whole spices up  to dry toasting them is the best way to  not just get the health benefits out of  the spice but also to get massive flavor  these ground coriander seeds are going  to give you these magical citrusy  peppery notes with a little bit of  crunch we're going to tip them into the  marinade for our salmon i'm adding olive  oil turmeric cinnamon cayenne pepper  garlic ginger and cumin i'm also adding  salt and pepper to taste all of these  spices not just boot gut health and  favorably interact with the microbiome  but they also fight inflammation this is  a marinade you can make and put on  anything i would put it on toast because  i'm the spice mama but you could put it  on chicken roast vegetables really  anything we're just gonna spoon this  marinade over our salmon salmon is  amazing for gut health because of the  omega-3 fatty acids found in salmon and  other types of fish these omega-3 fats  are also inflammation fighters and  studies have shown that salmon can  increase the diversity of the bugs in  our microbiome really nourishing the  good guys and keeping in check the not  so good ones hands down the most  effective way to nourish your microbiome  is to eat lots and lots of plant-based  foods like fruits vegetables legumes  lentils this is why we are adding  oranges and lemons to add not just gut  health boosting fiber but also  really delicious taste notes  [Music]  the easiest way to think of your gut  microbiome in health is to think of jedi  bugs and stormtrooper bugs the jedis  they're the good guys they keep you  healthy they fight off the storm  troopers and the stormtroopers well we  know what they do so  a great way to boost the jedi bugs is to  feed them foods that they love this  brings us to the dandelion greens which  we're cooking up today these greens  contain prebiotics which are food for  the probiotics so they really help those  jedi bacteria become strong and powerful  we're going to start with some olive oil  in a pan on medium heat to this olive  oil we're adding some onion  we're going to allow it to soften for a  few minutes the onion olive oil garlic  and lemon is really going to help to  counter those bitter notes in the  dandelion greens we're going to add the  garlic and just allow it to get fragrant  for about a minute we don't want to burn  the garlic we just want it to soften and  mellow out a great hack to extract the  maximum benefits from garlic is to chop  the garlic and let it sit for about 10  minutes before you add it to your dish  because this will allow allicin which is  a powerful anti-inflammatory compound to  get truly activated to the onion and  garlic we're going to add our gorgeous  dandelion greens  dandelion greens are particularly  powerful gut health boosting foods  because they contain a fiber called  inulin which is one of the most potent  prebiotic fibers out there okay they're  wilting beautifully and so we're just  gonna hit them with a little salt a  little pepper  and a generous squeeze of lemon juice  the lemon is not just going to help with  flavor but it's also going to help you  extract lots of micronutrients from the  greens okay  that is looking good we're going to  check on our salmon and complete our  dinner now that everything's done we  have our salmon we have our dandelion  greens and we've also plated it with our  sweet potato fries because plants fiber  color all going to benefit your gut  health okay so plating oh my god that  actually looks really good when using  salmon it's a really good idea when you  can to go with wild caught salmon over  farm salmon because not only is it  richer in omega-3 fats but it's also  lower in some organic pollutants this is  looking beautiful but we're not quite  finished we're gonna top this with some  more gut health boosting goodness first  up we have fresh cilantro just like we  have the coriander seeds we now have  fresh cilantro which has gut health  boosting antioxidant properties as well  next up sumac one of my favorite spices  of all time think of it as lemon without  the liquid  also powerful anti-inflammatory spice  and antioxidant rich spice and last but  not least the king of all gut health  boosting foods broccoli sprouts broccoli  sprouts contain a compound called  sulforaphane which is nature's most  powerful activator of anti-inflammatory  pathways in our body and also  antioxidants if you can't get your hand  on broccoli sprouts you could just  incorporate raw broccoli on a regular  basis in your diet we're just gonna top  our salmon with these anti-inflammatory  gut health boosting broccoli sprouts  which are also gonna give you this  mustardy peppery flavor after this we're  gonna get started with dessert where  we're gonna be cooking our spiced apple  crumble this dessert packs a bunch of  those beneficial prebiotic fibers to  boost the good bacteria and it's super  delicious in the bowl we have oat flour  which is a really good substitute for  all